You will get blasted (typically) only if you have an intelligent
artifact of wrong alignment, obtained from a bones heap or wished
for. What damage you can suffer from non-matching artifacts depends
on your character, stats and equipment. But as long as you have an
altar and can safely sacrifice for a divine gift, I'd do that until
something non-crappy appears at your feet. A gift will also free
the proficiency slot if not already available for your role. I'd
abtain from using weapons where you are restricted in. A wish for
an artifact, AFAIK, will not unrestrict your proficiency. I think
I've seen a list of good artifact weapons discussed in the NH-Wiki.

